<!--
    SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
    SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 BorderKeys contributors

    The two builds are separate packages and can be installed at the same time, so all three
    names a user is shown have to tell them apart: the launcher, the settings activity, and the
    input-method picker. Leaving any of them alone gives a list with two identical entries and
    no way to know which is which without opening one.

    The library modules own the last two, and an application's resources win over a library's,
    which is why they are overridden here rather than in a flavour of each module.
-->
<resources>
    <string name="app_name" translatable="false">BorderKeys +</string>
    <string name="settings_activity_label" translatable="false">BorderKeys +</string>
    <string name="ime_name" translatable="false">BorderKeys +</string>
</resources>
